# Mosquitto ACL scaffold for the Multi-Bus Gateway bundled stack.
#
# WHY: with `mqtt.allow_write_entities` on, whoever can publish to
# `<prefix>/cmd/#`, the HA `.../set` topics or `mbg/rules/+/set` can act on
# hardware. The gateway cannot see WHO published — the broker's ACL is the
# authentication (security-hardening.md §4). Out of the box every consumer
# shares one user with full publish rights; this file splits that into a
# read-only telemetry account and named accounts for the writers.
#
# ACTIVATE:
#   1) copy:    cp acl.example acl            (same directory, mounted :ro)
#   2) enable:  add `acl_file /mosquitto/config/acl` to mosquitto.conf
#   3) users:   add the extra users on the DATA volume (they survive restarts;
#               the first user is re-written from .env each start):
#                 docker exec -it mbg-mosquitto \
#                   mosquitto_passwd /mosquitto/data/passwd mbg-telemetry
#                 docker exec -it mbg-mosquitto \
#                   mosquitto_passwd /mosquitto/data/passwd mbg-control
#   4) restart the mosquitto container.
#
# Mosquitto semantics: `write` = publish, `read` = subscribe. Once an
# acl_file is set, anything not matched is DENIED for that user.

# ── the gateway itself (MQTT_USERNAME from .env) ─────────────────────────────
# Publishes all telemetry/discovery and subscribes its own command topics.
# Replace `mbg` with your MQTT_USERNAME.
user mbg
topic readwrite #

# ── read-only consumers: dashboards, Telegraf, MQTT Explorer ────────────────
# Telemetry in, nothing out. Point Home Assistant here too if you do not use
# the HA write entities.
user mbg-telemetry
topic read #

# ── controllers: Node-RED, Home Assistant with write entities ───────────────
# Everything readable, publish ONLY on the write faces they drive. Narrow the
# patterns to your real topic prefixes (config-reference.md: topic patterns);
# `%c`/`%u` substitution is also available for per-client trees.
user mbg-control
topic read #
# template commands (mqtt-contract.md §Commands): <dev or group prefix>/cmd/<name>
topic write +/cmd/+
topic write +/+/cmd/+
# HA write entities (…/set under a unit prefix) — only with allow_write_entities
topic write +/+/set
topic write +/+/+/set
# rule control (disable / clamp / override; arming stays API/UI-only)
topic write mbg/rules/+/set
